### F1 (LOW): two PerLTQA snapshots blended in one argument

check_corpora.py reads `cache_arch_eval.pkl` (30 archives, 12288 docs); check_decisive §C reads `cache_items.json` (31 archives, 12323 docs). CRITIQUE sec 1b takes sizes from the first and text stats from the second without noting the different cohorts (delta 1 archive / 35 docs / 0.3%). Both scripts are faithful to their inputs; FINDINGS_DIGEST's "30/12288" matches the eval cache. No published number wrong; state the two-cache fact when combining the stat blocks.

### F2 (LOW): two banding rules (rare 341 vs 412)

Brain rule gives 7/133/153/412; the digest stratification table gives 24/224/116/341. The digest discloses both rules and the defended claim (rare n=412, +4.78) uses the brain's rule — self-consistent. Hazard only: never join brain's both-miss-by-band with the digest's CODE-vs-BM25-by-band row-for-row.

### F3 (MED): CRITIQUE sec 1a grades against coarse BM25

"Float loses by 5.67pp" uses frozen coarse BM25 54.18; the decision round set fair BM25 at 61.70 (+6.38, brief §C). Under the fair baseline the deficit roughly doubles. Verdict survives a fortiori — but "5.67pp" is stale and must not be quoted against the fair baseline.

### F4 (LOW): tie conventions (46.68 vs 46.52)

Brain's compare block uses expected-tie 46.68 (HATA convention); frozen deterministic is 46.5248 (LADDER.json). Brain's oracle arithmetic closes internally. Never difference the two conventions; already-listed known issue class.

